## Fix the Manual Mapping panel hanging on the Mapping tab

Context: Issue #145 — in Manual Mapping, clicking a mapped entity and opening the
rightmost "Mapping" tab showed the spinner forever. The bottom panel reuses the
Designer's entity/relationship panel (`loadEntityPanelContent()` /
`loadRelationshipPanelContent()` rendered into `#manualPanelBody`), but the
Designer's preview query discards its response unless `currentPanelType` says an
entity/relationship panel is open. Only `openEntityMappingFromDesign()` /
`openRelationshipMappingFromDesign()` ever set it, so from Manual Mapping the flag
stayed `null`: `/mapping/test-query` returned 200, the result was dropped, and
`#epMappingLoading` was never hidden. Second latent defect on the same path — the
panel markup uses page-global `ep*` / `rp*` element ids and both hosts live in the
DOM at once, so a leftover copy in the Designer panel shadowed the Manual one on
every `getElementById` lookup.

Backport of the develop fix (cherry-pick of 2f796c1).

Changes:

1. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   Added panel-ownership tracking: `currentPanelHostId` plus `claimMappingPanel()`,
   `releaseMappingPanel()` and `closeActiveMappingPanel()`. Claiming records the
   host that received the markup and closes the other host, so only one copy of the
   `ep*` / `rp*` ids exists. `closeMappingPanel()` now delegates its reset to
   `releaseMappingPanel()` instead of repeating it.
2. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   `loadEntityPanelContent()` and `loadRelationshipPanelContent()` claim the panel
   before initialising it, so the preview query started by `initEntityPanel()` /
   `initRelationshipPanel()` passes the stale-response guard whichever host
   rendered it.
3. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   `_pollAndSaveResult()` closes the owning host via `closeActiveMappingPanel()`;
   Manual Mapping's Auto-Map shares that poll loop and previously left its panel
   open with stale content.
4. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-manual.js
   `ManualModule.closePanel()` releases the shared panel (cancelling any in-flight
   preview query) and no longer assumes the manual DOM is present, since the
   Designer side can now call it.
5. tests/units/front/test_manual_mapping_panel_host.py
   New source-contract regression covering claim/release/close dispatch and pinning
   the stale-response guards that make ownership mandatory. 11 of its 13 tests fail
   without the fix.

